Third-party material
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This product includes material adapted from FastChat
(https://github.com/lm-sys/FastChat), Copyright the FastChat authors,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. FastChat does not ship a
NOTICE file at the referenced commit, so no upstream NOTICE text is carried
over.

Referenced FastChat revision: commit 587d5cfa1609a43d192cedb8441cac3c17db105d
(fschat 0.2.36).

1. Judge prompt wording (src/judge_adapter/prompt.py, src/judge_adapter/user_prompt.py)
   The default pairwise judge instructions are adapted from the MT-Bench
   pairwise judge prompts in fastchat/llm_judge/data/judge_prompts.jsonl
   ("pair-v2" and "pair-v2-multi-turn"), e.g. "act as an impartial judge",
   "follows the user's instructions and answers the user's question better",
   "helpfulness, relevance, accuracy, depth, creativity, and level of detail",
   the position / length / name bias sentences and "Be as objective as
   possible". The "### User:" / "### Assistant:" conversation rendering
   follows the multi-turn template of the same file.
   Changes: reworded; assistants are referred to by field name; the
   explanation and the "[[A]]"/"[[B]]"/"[[C]]" verdict format are removed;
   the output is a single option id; question and conversations are sent as
   separate named fields. The rubric / reference / data-handling sentences of
   user_prompt.py are new.
   The prompts are described in: Zheng et al., "Judging LLM-as-a-Judge with
   MT-Bench and Chatbot Arena", arXiv:2306.05685 (2023).

2. FastChat host binding (src/judge_adapter/hosts/fastchat.py,
   src/judge_adapter/fastchat_runner.py) - optional, extra "fastchat"
   These modules contain no FastChat source code. They import FastChat at run
   time, replace fastchat.llm_judge.common.run_judge_pair /
   run_judge_single with functions that follow FastChat's call signature and
   return contract, run FastChat's own gen_judgment.py / show_result.py, and
   mirror the command-line option names of gen_judgment.py for validation.
   The FastChat demo copies FastChat's own data files from the user's
   FastChat installation or checkout at run time; no FastChat data (MT-Bench
   questions, reference answers or judge prompts) is distributed with this
   product.

FastChat itself is not bundled. Installing the optional "fastchat" extra
downloads FastChat and its dependencies under their own licenses.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Models and services
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No model weights are distributed. The "haiku_direct" backend calls the
Anthropic Messages API and the "choice_endpoint" backend calls a RunPod serverless
endpoint that the user configures; both require the user's own account and
API key and are subject to those providers' terms.
